  "id": "DrugBank_DB14031 - MONDO_6335",
  "verbalization": "Tretamine appears to be linked to Ovarian Endometrioid Adenocarcinoma through a series of indications involving Melphalan and Hydroxyurea. The evidence suggests that Tretamine may act as a potential therapeutic agent for ovarian tumors, as it is associated with malignancies such as Malignant Non-dysgerminomatous and Malignant Dysgerminomatous Germ Cell Tumors of Ovary, both of which are classified under the broader category of Ovarian Endometrioid Adenocarcinoma. This connection implies a possible role for Tretamine in the treatment of this cancer type, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The presence of Melphalan, a known chemotherapy agent, in the pathway suggests a possible synergistic relationship between Tretamine and Melphalan, which may contribute to the progression or treatment of Ovarian Endometrioid Adenocarcinoma. The evidence highlights a potential pathway where Tretamine could influence the tumor's progression, though further investigation is needed to elucidate the precise mechanism of action.",
